#X text 240 83 WebSocket is a protocol that provides full-duplex communication
channels over a single TCP connection \, widely used in web applications
for real-time data exchange;
#X text 240 138 the object starts a WebSocket server \, accepts client
connections and exchanges text \, binary or JSON messages with them;
#X text 240 193 the second outlet outputs the list CLIENT_ID CLIENT_ADDR
when a client connects or disconnects;
#X text 240 233 most methods take a TARGET selector to address one
\, all or a subset of clients;
#X text 50 336 you can start testing websocket client with command:
'websocat ws://127.0.0.1:8000';
